{"verdicts":[{"coverage":{"complete":true,"interactions":["core.js check(): verification waiver (waiverFor in contracts.js:182-189) interacts with verificationCoverage, CI qualification and the hostedCi exact-head check; a finding-scoped waiver needs a FAIL result, so it never covers a PASS outcome's coverage gaps (verified)","core.js check() outcomes consumed by delegation.js applyDelegation (lines 438-449) and the standing/delegated merge/completion checks via autonomous.js allowedRunOutcome: waived residuals counted as PASS (finding F1)","core.js check() outcomes consumed by final-handoff.js PR explainer (lines 97-136): waivedCoverage not shown (finding F2)","core.js decide(): pendingDecision identity checked before value.observed is added, so retries of the same operation stay stable; observed comes from the same admission check","core.js commitments()/authorizedBriefSubject with delegation.js briefScope/briefScopeChanged/assertBriefScopeUnchanged: a log-only change keeps the subject; a scope change gives a fresh subject, a missing authorization and a delegated hand-back; unreadable or changed-while-reading briefs fail closed","core.js prepare()/check(): the candidate still pins the exact brief bytes; candidate.authorization.subject matches the carried subject","workspace.js observeDelivery -> observeFeatureBase -> minimalConfiguration -> context.js featureBaseSha validation (lowercase full hex) -> evidence.js:191/249 FEATURE base check","Desktop copies vs canonical plugin-src protocol (parity receipt)","Mandate constraint: boundary-review.js, execution.js and the BOUNDARY_REVIEWED reducer (core.js:126) are unchanged; base and head line counts are identical"],"limitations":[],"paths":["repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/core.js","repository/apps/desktop/resources/protocol/current/core.js","repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/workspace.js","repository/apps/desktop/resources/protocol/current/workspace.js","repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/PROTOCOL.md","repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/commands/light-run.md","repository/cli/test/current-waivers.test.js","repository/cli/test/current-workspace-config.test.js"]},"coverageDecisions":[],"criteria":[{"evidence":"cli/test/current-waivers.test.js:38-68 runs for light and full. It builds a reused narrower verification with an UNAVAILABLE reviewer (`pairedAdapters(f, { unavailable: 'claude-code' })`), checks that acceptance is first blocked with 'uncovered prior behavior', records `waive` of review and verification with actions ['accept'], and asserts `after.allowed === true` and a successful `milestone.pass` acceptance. Receipt sha256:72e6bc02… shows both 'light: …' and 'full: …' ok on head 0f0e5fa. The implementation is in core.js:1136-1143 and core.js:546-547.","id":"R1","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"current-waivers.test.js:53-67 asserts: review outcome UNAVAILABLE with an exception; verification outcome PASS with an exception and one waivedCoverage entry matching 'uncovered prior behavior'; `recorded.observed.review.outcome` UNAVAILABLE; `observed.verification.outcome` PASS with waivedCoverage; the MILESTONE payload outcomes keep review UNAVAILABLE and verification waivedCoverage. The implementation is in core.js:549-559 (observed) and core.js:1231 (MILESTONE outcomes from check). Receipt passed.","id":"R2","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"current-waivers.test.js:70-80: a review-only waive-and-accept is rejected with /Required review proof is missing: .*uncovered prior behavior/. Acceptance stays blocked naming the coverage residual, and `waivedCoverage` is undefined without a verification waiver. The implementation is in core.js:547 (refusal now includes `admission.missing`) and core.js:1137-1139 (no exception, so `missing`). Receipt passed.","id":"R3","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"current-waivers.test.js:84-110 covers four cases. A findings-log append keeps `commitments().subject`, the implementation milestone is allowed, `candidate.prepare` succeeds and pins the logged brief, and there is still one authorize-implementation. A nested '### Round 2' heading in the log keeps the subject. A scope edit changes the subject, blocks the implementation milestone ('current implementation authorization') and refuses candidate.prepare. Restoring the scope restores the subject. The implementation is in core.js:358-384 using delegation.js briefScope:327-336, failing closed on read errors and on bytes that change during the read. Receipts: waivers, light (e104f837…) and delegation (c4383bdc…) passed.","id":"R4","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"current-workspace-config.test.js:399-429 (full and light) moves main past the fork point. It asserts that `featureBaseSha` equals the merge base `f.base`, that the STARTED record has observed.featureBase {sha, ref:'refs/remotes/origin/main'}, and that FEATURE `candidate.prepare` with base f.base succeeds with no hand edit. Lines 431-443 cover the unresolvable case: no featureBaseSha, and the reason is recorded. Updated expectations at lines 86-87, 96 and 385. The implementation is in workspace.js:106-131. Receipt 0d6ff5f9… shows all 18 cases ok, including both featureBaseSha tests.","id":"R5","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"The parity receipt 65ceee6c… shows 'CLI, desktop, MCP and plugin copies match and use contract gatereeve/current/8'. Plugin validate and validate-native receipts passed. Focused suites (waivers, light, workspace-config, delegation, core) passed on 0f0e5fa. The full `npm test --prefix cli` was not run locally. It is covered by the planned required CI check 'Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 acceptance', which runs ci/portable-acceptance.sh:21 `npm test --prefix cli`, and will be qualified after convergence. That suite result is not yet observed and is not claimed as passed here.","id":"R6","outcome":"PASS"}],"dimensions":[{"evidence":"Correct: waiverFor binding is reused (subject or applicability, risk hash, policy); a finding-scoped verification waiver cannot cover PASS coverage gaps (contracts.js:187); observed is added after the pendingDecision identity check, so retries are stable; authorizedBriefSubject fails closed (core.js:378-383); observeFeatureBase validates the hex SHA and prefers the remote-tracking ref without fetching (workspace.js:114-124); context.js:229-237 accepts the written lowercase SHA. Defect F1 (medium, blocking): core.js:1136-1140 keeps verification at PASS while hiding residuals, and autonomous.js:102 allowedRunOutcome, used by delegation.js:439 and core.js:1192/1198, therefore counts a waived verification as an exception-free PASS. Low F2: final-handoff.js:122-136 does not show waivedCoverage.","name":"code","outcome":"FAIL"},{"evidence":"R1–R5 are each demonstrated by the named tests in cli/test/current-waivers.test.js and current-workspace-config.test.js, with passing receipts on 0f0e5fa. R6: the parity receipt passed and the full suite is planned in CI (portable-acceptance.sh:21). Design choices 1–3 in requirements/design.md match the implementation, and PROTOCOL.md:81-90 and 171-179 and light-run.md:52-57 document them. Project rules: the protocol source is plugin-src with a matching desktop copy (parity test), and the contract stays gatereeve/current/8.","name":"requirements","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"Eight agent-run receipts, all exit 0 with evaluatedSource 0f0e5fa (runner 70904c70…, environmentCheck unchanged). Together they cover every changed source area: core waiver/coverage (current-core, current-waivers), light commitments (current-light, current-waivers, current-delegation for the briefScope hand-back), workspace (current-workspace-config), the desktop copies (parity test) and plugin validation. Both changed test suites (current-waivers new, current-workspace-config modified) were run. The implementer's alternative validation scope is an adequate local basis. The ciRequiredChecks (Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 acceptance and container, Desktop contract 22.04/24.04) cover the approved scope: