mous.js:102 `allowedRunOutcome` returns true for `outcome.outcome === 'PASS'` without checking exception or waivedCoverage. delegation.js:439-440 requires `check.allowed && every allowedRunOutcome` under the message 'Delegated acceptance requires current PASS evidence for every required gate (no exceptions)'. delegation.js:448-449 records gates as {id, outcome, result} with the reason 'every required gate passed'. core.js:1191-1192 and 1197-1198 apply the same `allowedRunOutcome` test to standing or delegated acceptance and merge. Human `waive` decisions do not hand delegation back (core.js:579-585). In base (core.js:1104-1150) these failures always went to `missing`, so this state was unreachable. design.md says 'No integrity, truth or authority rule is weakened'. No test covers delegated or standing acceptance with a waived residual.","failureScenario":"In a delegated or mandated SLICE run in this hosted-CI repository, the verification is local-only or CI is reused, so coverage or CI qualification is unmet. A human records `waive` of verification without `accept`. The agent then calls `delegation.apply`. `check('acceptance')` is allowed, because the residuals went to `waivedCoverage` instead of `missing`. `allowedRunOutcome` sees verification outcome PASS. The protocol appends a delegated `accept` whose reason is 'every required gate passed' and whose gates[] carry no exception or waivedCoverage. The documented '(no exceptions)' delegated acceptance rule is bypassed and the record overstates success. Standing or delegated merge/completion checks are bypassed the same way.","id":"F1","path":"repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/core.js","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":false,"classId":"waived-residual-hidden-in-human-view","classStatement":"The human-facing PR explainer omits the waived coverage residuals that the record retains.","criterion":"gate:review","evidence":"final-handoff.js:122-125 builds exceptions from `row.exception` reason and consequences only. final-handoff.js:136 renders verification rows as `${row.outcome} · ${row.reason}`. `waivedCoverage` is not read anywhere in final-handoff.js. The file is unchanged by this candidate. This is a presentation gap next to the new honest-record behaviour, not a requirement breach: R2 requires the MILESTONE and decision records, which do hold the residuals.","failureScenario":"After a waive-and-accept with waivedCoverage, `review.publish` generates the PR explainer. Its Verification section shows 'PASS · <reason>' and its Acceptance decisions section shows only the decision's reason and consequences. The skipped prior behaviour is not shown to a human reading the PR, although the journal records it.","id":"F2","path":"repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/final-handoff.js","severity":"low"}],"gate":"review","historyAssessment":null,"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"Goal: #145 items 1–3 are all built in one change set: waiver past coverage recorded honestly (core.js:1132-1143, 549-559), findings-log growth without re-authorization (core.js:358-384), and run.start writing featureBaseSha (workspace.js:110-131). Each is tested (R1–R5). Constraint 1, staying out of the #140 reviewer pipeline, holds: boundary-review.js (309 lines) and execution.js (1067 lines) are line-for-line the same length in base and head, and the BOUNDARY_REVIEWED reducer case (core.js:126) and GOAL_READY_STALE set are unchanged. The core.js edits are only in commitments, decide and the post-outcome verification checks. Constraint 2, public PR/issue text, cannot be fully verified because no PR text is in the evidence. Source comments cite only 'GitHub issue #145' and name no local paths or other projects (the local paths seen are in runner receipts, not public text). Constraint 3, no merge without the human: nothing in the change performs or authorizes a merge. mandateAuthority is human-confirmed ('Proceed' on the fixed mandate).","outcome":"PASS"},"outcome":"FAIL","summary":"I reviewed the complete FEATURE change, head 0f0e5fa against base/target e59b02c, and the review does not pass. The three #145 items are built, tested and meet R1–R6. One medium-severity defect blocks under the round-1 band: the waiver change weakens the rule that delegated and standing acceptance must have every required gate PASS with no exceptions.\n\nWhat changed and how each part holds up:\n- Waivers (core.js check/decide): a current human verification waiver now covers the coverage, assessed-evidence/CI-qualification and hosted-CI exact-head checks. Each skipped check is kept as `waivedCoverage` on the verification outcome and in the acceptance MILESTONE record. A `waive` decision now records `observed`, and the waive-and-accept refusal names what is missing.\n- Findings log (core.js `authorizedBriefSubject`): a light run keeps its authorized subject while only the findings log changes.\n- Feature base (workspace.js `observeFeatureBase`/`minimalConfiguration`): `run.start` writes `featureBaseSha` from `git merge-base` with no fetch, or records why it could not.\n- Docs and copies: PROTOCOL.md and light-run.md are updated, and the desktop copies match.\n\nThe defect: the waiver keeps the verification outcome as PASS. `allowedRunOutcome` (autonomous.js:102) only checks `outcome === 'PASS'`, so `delegation.apply` (delegation.js:439-449) and the standing/delegated checks at merge and completion (core.js:1191-1192, 1197-1198) now count a waived verification as passing. Before this change that state was always blocked.\n\nAlso found, low and not blocking: the PR explainer leaves out `waivedCoverage`.\n\nCaveats:\n- The full `npm test --prefix cli` suite was not run locally. It is deferred to the planned hosted CI, whose 'Ubuntu acceptance' job runs it through ci/portable-acceptance.sh:21.\n- PR text is not in the evidence, so the public-text constraint could not be observed directly.\n- No changed-path list was supplied. I found the changed files by comparing the base and head trees."}]}